    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        2575.114501953125,
        2182.365478515625
      ],
      "size": [
        429.703125,
        149.703125
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MODEL STACK\n==========================\nBase model : Minimax-h3_Singularity_ref2va_v1.3_int8  (ref2v fine-tune)\nLoRA       : minimax_h3_ref2v_turbo_4step_v0.1   strength 1.0\nSampling   : BasicScheduler (beta, adjustable steps) + euler\nMode       : SINGLE pass  — one sampling pass, no second pass\n\n* Singularity pairs with the 4-step v0.1 LoRA only. Don't swap in the 8-step LoRA.\n* Singularity is a reference-to-video specialist. For plain image-to-video,\n  use a hybrid base model instead."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 34,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        2414.253662109375,
        2401.242431640625
      ],
      "size": [
        619.921875,
        679.765625
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "H3 LONG TAKE — Motion Context V2 (local)\n==========================================\n\nSAMPLING\n  sampling_mode = single     <- NOT dual. This is the whole trick.\n  Tested: continuing a chain off dual-pass latents gives pixel shift at\n  the joins. Single pass joins clean. For long takes, always single.\n  1st_pass_only / disable_2nd_noise only affect the second pass.\n  In single mode they do nothing — leave them.\n\nSTEPS (green BasicScheduler node)\n  8   default. Dancing, fast hands, busy backgrounds, walking + talking\n  6   low motion: talking head, slow walk, locked camera\n  4   runs, but dialogue drops syllables. Only with no speech.\n\nRESOLUTION\n  1.0 MP  fast, safe default for iteration\n  1.4 MP  up to ~10 s per segment on a 24-32 GB card\n  Past ~1.2-1.4 MP you mostly buy size, not detail.\n  VRAM rule of thumb: frames x megapixels <= ~540 per segment.\n\nMULTI-TRACK EDITOR\n  Segment 1 = \"shot\".  Every later segment = \"context\".\n  ref_image_size = max\n  Put the reference image on segment 1 -> hover it -> Share icon ->\n  \"Use as shared reference\". Later segments inherit it automatically.\n\nPROJECT SETTINGS (Multi-Track Project node)\n  project_name          always name it (empty = \"default\")\n  segment_start_number  counts from 1\n  segment_count         -1 = from start segment to the end\n  Re-render ONE segment: start = N, count = 1  (local only —\n  the saved context latents live in output/easy_media/projects/<name>/)\n\nPROMPTS\n  - A context segment's timestamps land ~0.92 s early in the final\n    video (22 pinned frames are trimmed). Write T + 0.92 to land at T.\n  - Open every context segment with CONTINUATION only — same pace,\n    same camera, same light — and zero scenery nouns.\n  - Never carry a progressive camera move across a join.\n  - Put joins mid-walk / mid-climb, never on a doorway or threshold.\n  - Dialogue: ~one short line every 2.5 s. Split between sentences."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
